n risk of the beef it replaced. Your skepticism isn’t irrational fear—it’s a self-protective instinct shaped by a hundred-year pattern of industry and regulatory failures. That instinct is a feature, not a bug. The best anyone can do is acknowledge the pattern, be transparent about what we do and don’t know, and empower you to make a personal risk calculation based on that transparency. You’re right to demand that, and right to be cautious.
